DeepSeek V3.2 is the clearest demonstration of why the third evaluation layer was necessary. On absolute scores all four conditions are compressed into a 0.03-point band (Table~\ref{tab:deepseek-results}); the judge returns literally identical scores for most sessions. Yet the paired total-score test already detects a significant Dissonance$-$Baseline advantage ($+0.16$, $t = 2.18$), and the pairwise layer resolves it decisively: net win-rate $0.660$ with 46 wins, 40 ties, 14 losses (sign-test $p = 0.00004$). A real, statistically robust preference exists that the absolute scale cannot express --- direct evidence of the LLM-judge generosity effect documented for psychotherapy evaluation by Haydarov et al.\ \cite{haydarov-etal-2025-towards}.

